# save-dialog-repro.rin - evidence script for the two save-dialog display bugs.
# Drives the ScummVM GUI SaveLoadChooser (GRID variant, the default) through the
# real user flow: F5 -> grid chooser -> click "New Save" -> SavenameDialog ->
# type name -> Enter. The .rin driver ticks inside the GuiManager loop; while
# the GUI is active, injected mouse coords are read as OVERLAY pixels (clamped
# to 320x200, which still reaches the top-left "New Save" tile).
# snap grabs the OVERLAY BUFFER at execution time - the evidence surface for
# both bugs.
wait 5000                       # boot + save-restore settle
state
snap pre-dialog                 # baseline: enhanced scene
key f5                          # SCI0 Save Game shortcut -> kSaveGame -> GUI grid chooser
wait 2500                       # dialog appear settle
snap grid                       # full-screen grid chooser (opaque; backdrop not visible here)
click 160 100                   # "New Save" tile (overlay px while GUI active)
wait 1200                       # grid session closes, SavenameDialog session opens
snap name-dialog                # BUG 1 evidence: backdrop behind the type-a-name dialog
type "rogertest"
key enter                       # OK -> save -> dialog closes, game resumes
wait 1500                       # deliberately NO mouse move
snap post-close-still           # BUG 2 evidence: stale dialog pixels, zero input
state
move 160 100
wait 400
snap post-close-after-move      # pre-fix: only cursor rects updated
quit
